{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"OpenUSD"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Getting Started In C++"},"abstract":[{"text":"Using SwiftUsd from C++","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Getting Started","level":2,"anchor":"Getting-Started","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Before you can start using SwiftUsd, you need to add it as a dependency to your Xcode project or Swift Package, and then configure a few build settings."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Despite the fact that SwiftUsd is a Swift Package, you can use it in a pure-C++ Xcode project\/target, as well as in a pure-C++ Swift Package target."}]}],"type":"aside"},{"name":"Important","style":"important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift Package targets cannot mix Swift and C++ code in a single target. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-package-manager\/issues\/8945","type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To do so, follow the steps in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/GettingStarted#Getting-Started","isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"Getting Started for Swift","type":"text"}],"overridingTitle":"Getting Started for Swift"},{"type":"text","text":". If you’re using a pure-C++ target, you don’t need to change the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C++ and Objective-C Interoperability"},{"type":"text","text":" mode in Xcode or add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".interoperabilityMode(.Cxx)"},{"type":"text","text":" to your target’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swiftSettings"},{"type":"text","text":" in your Swift Package manifest."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Using SwiftUsd","level":3,"anchor":"Using-SwiftUsd","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Once you’ve added SwiftUsd as a package dependency to your Xcode project or Swift package and set the C++ version to GNU++17, you’re ready to start using SwiftUsd:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"c++","code":["#include <iostream>","#include \"pxr\/usd\/usd\/stage.h\"","#include \"pxr\/usd\/usd\/prim.h\"","#include \"pxr\/usd\/usdGeom\/tokens.h\"","","std::string makeHelloWorldString() {","    pxr::UsdStageRefPtr stage = pxr::UsdStage::CreateInMemory();","    stage->DefinePrim(pxr::SdfPath(\"\/hello\"), pxr::UsdGeomTokens->Cube);","    stage->DefinePrim(pxr::SdfPath(\"\/hello\/world\"), pxr::UsdGeomTokens->Sphere);","    std::string result;","    stage->ExportToString(&result);","    return result;","}","","int main(int argc, const char * argv[]) {","    std::cout << makeHelloWorldString() << std::endl;","    return 0;","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To use new functions or types added by SwiftUsd, include the SwiftUsd umbrella header:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"c++","code":["#include \"swiftUsd\/swiftUsd.h\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This header lets you use macros useful for Swift-Cxx interop, functions that are important for memory safety with Swift-Cxx interop, and Swift wrapper types for C++ types not imported by Swift-Cxx interop.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t include other files in ","type":"text"},{"code":"OpenUSD\/swiftUsd","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as they are implementation details and may change without warning","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftusd\/gettingstartedincplusplus"]},{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftusd\/gettingstartedincplusplus"]}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["d